package views

// analytics renders the site's third-party analytics tag into a document head.
// It is the single place any tracker is mounted, shared by all three self-
// contained documents (Layout, LandingPage, SandboxesPage) so the snippet is
// written once rather than copied into three heads that would then drift.
//
// It renders NOTHING when no client id is configured. That is the common case
// for a self-hosted or local-mode install, a test run and a dev box, and none of
// them should ship a beacon to a vendor: tracking is opt-in, enabled only by
// setting OPENPANEL_CLIENT_ID.
//
// The snippet is emitted via templ.Raw because templ does not evaluate
// expressions inside a literal <script> tag — see openPanelScript, which builds
// the whole element (and escapes the id) for exactly that reason.
templ analytics() {
	if OpenPanelClientID != "" {
		@templ.Raw(openPanelScript(OpenPanelClientID))
	}
}
